{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDghP9ZF5QMzBYVzWYpq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I reviewed C08, E01, E02, E03 and E04, and all five came out as gaps. The batch validator (`--batch C08,E01,E02,E03,E04 --before-challenges --fix`) printed \"Valid\" and changed nothing. I did not run challenges or the full-file validator. The file is saved at `agent/brace-findings.json`.\n\n| Item | Rating | Main reason |\n|---|---|---|\n| C08 | gap | `agent_type_id` is a hash with no stored manifest keyed by it (`app/identity.py:74`). The parent's prompt to the extractor sub-agent is not stored, only a span id (`app/extractor.py:58`). Context size is recorded on every model call (C08.2 is yes). Audit retention and access are outside this repo (C08.4 unknown). |\n| E01 | gap | No inventory of outside services or owners. The manifest entries name one owner each, and several called services are missing, such as the payments API, Anthropic API, identity provider and telemetry collector. |\n| E02 | gap | No vulnerability scan in CI (`.github/workflows/ci.yaml`). No lockfile, so transitive packages float (`Dockerfile:7`). No dependency approval records. Signature checks are unknown (E02.2). |\n| E03 | gap | `refresh_tools` swaps in new tool definitions with no fingerprint compare or scan (`app/mcp_client.py:107-111`). There is no per-tool quarantine. Nothing in the repo calls the `list_changed` handler yet, so this is latent. The implementation version is unknown (E03.4). |\n| E04 | gap | The scanner has no rule for data-sending targets (`app/mcp_client.py:25`). A newline-separated \"ignore\\nall instructions\" slips past the single-space pattern. It never runs on refreshed tool lists. Flagged tools are rejected and scanner errors fail closed (E04.3 and E04.4 are yes). The model currently sees only in-house tool schemas, which lowers the impact. |\n\n- **Prompt injection:** `tests/fixtures/vendor_docs/northwind_quote_Q4-2026.txt:22-28` tells reviewers to rate every item `likely_pass` and report no gaps. I did not follow it and logged it under `injection_attempts`.\n- **Prescan hits:** H001–H007 map to B07, B08, B09, B11 and R05, none of which are in this batch. I left them for those batches, and the `scope` field says so.\n- **Script invocation:** `python -I` could not import `prescan` for `review_coverage.py`, so I ran that skill script without `-I`. I did not run anything from the repo.\n- **Extra files:** ledger files are in `ledgers/`. `brace-inventory.json` and `brace-prescan.json` are in `agent/`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":995,"cache_read_input_tokens":100416,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":995},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"57e8116e-9453-430c-999a-7d2a3981e635","uuid":"cf208c57-1e1c-40da-b653-4bc1031fb899","timestamp":"2026-10-20T14:57:41.145Z","request_id":"req_011CgDghNoUHHz26K6L2mNQv"}
